  "question": {
    "html": "<p>Two blocks, <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Y\"></span>, of masses <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"m\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2m\"></span> respectively, are held together with a compressed spring between them on a frictionless horizontal surface.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>When the blocks are released, the spring pushes them apart. How do the magnitude of the change in momentum and the final kinetic energy compare for blocks <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Y\"></span>?</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th></th><th>Magnitude of the change in momentum</th><th>Final kinetic energy</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr data-label=\"A\"><td>A.</td><td>same for <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Y\"></span></td><td>same for <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Y\"></span></td></tr><tr data-label=\"B\"><td>B.</td><td>greater for <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Y\"></span> than <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span></td><td>same for <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Y\"></span></td></tr><tr data-label=\"C\"><td>C.</td><td>same for <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Y\"></span></td><td>greater for <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span> than <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Y\"></span></td></tr><tr data-label=\"D\"><td>D.</td><td>greater for <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Y\"></span> than <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span></td><td>greater for <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span> than <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Y\"></span></td></tr></tbody></table>"
  },
